WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.617 --> 00:00:02.169
- This is my father Sasha.

00:00:02.169 --> 00:00:03.904
A lot of you don't know my dad.

00:00:03.904 --> 00:00:05.539
I love my dad very, very much.

00:00:05.539 --> 00:00:07.744
Gotten some interesting comments

00:00:07.744 --> 00:00:10.353
from the Larry King 
episode that I did.

00:00:10.353 --> 00:00:11.018
You know, they're like,

00:00:11.018 --> 00:00:12.733
"Oh, you really give 
your dad some good daps,"

00:00:12.733 --> 00:00:16.029
and, you know, it's funny 
my kids are getting older and

00:00:16.029 --> 00:00:20.554
I'm becoming a more experienced
dad and I think that you know,

00:00:20.554 --> 00:00:25.359
obviously, we got to know each
other in the late 90s and early

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:28.587
2000's because you 
just worked so hard.

00:00:28.587 --> 00:00:29.587
And I thank you for that, Dad.

00:00:29.587 --> 00:00:33.058
I thank you so much for
sacrificing and I know you did

00:00:33.058 --> 00:00:36.628
it in a selfish way 'cause 
I do it too in a selfish way.

00:00:36.628 --> 00:00:39.564
I know that it's your natural
state to be an entrepreneur

00:00:39.564 --> 00:00:40.752
and build for yourself.

00:00:40.752 --> 00:00:43.969
But it doesn't take away from 
the fact of what you did and

00:00:43.969 --> 00:00:46.275
what you established and how you

00:00:46.275 --> 00:00:48.340
started the process of 
our family being here.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.520
Not only did you but 
you brought the whole family

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.658
along with you including your
mom and your grandparents and

00:00:55.658 --> 00:00:59.811
you came to this country
and you worked so damn hard.

00:01:01.101 --> 00:01:04.304
You know it's funny, I think
through all our frictions in

00:01:04.304 --> 00:01:08.275
building the business, it's
super easy and has always been

00:01:08.275 --> 00:01:11.778
super easy for me to focus on
how we're different and what

00:01:11.778 --> 00:01:15.782
I don't agree on but I've been
noticing a trend especially

00:01:15.782 --> 00:01:20.454
maybe because I don't see you
every day like I used to and

00:01:20.454 --> 00:01:22.689
I'm not around as much on a

00:01:22.689 --> 00:01:26.159
everyday basis with 
you but it's been

00:01:26.159 --> 00:01:30.998
interesting to me over the last
24 months, 36 months to start

00:01:30.998 --> 00:01:33.109
being more in tune than ever

00:01:33.109 --> 00:01:36.637
with not our differences 
but our similarities.

00:01:36.637 --> 00:01:41.108
Back in the day, in the late 90s
or early 2000s, I really thought

00:01:41.108 --> 00:01:44.411
that I was 90% mom and 10% you.

00:01:44.411 --> 00:01:46.926
And that's really just because
I didn't know you as well, Dad.

00:01:46.926 --> 00:01:49.431
It's funny to me to recognize

00:01:49.431 --> 00:01:52.287
how much more similar 
I am to you than I realized.

00:01:52.287 --> 00:01:55.802
And, you know, I just want you
to know how much you mean to me

00:01:55.802 --> 00:01:59.134
and even though 
I think for a long time

00:01:59.134 --> 00:02:01.154
in my 20s and 30s that

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:03.936
my own ego and my own pride

00:02:03.936 --> 00:02:06.626
was so scared 
for the narrative to

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.259
be that you're the reason 
I was successful.

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:12.598
That you're, even to this day, 
Dad, I know you

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:14.601
don't read the 
comments on the internet.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.248
You'd find it interesting 
how many people in a

00:02:16.248 --> 00:02:19.536
YouTube comment will say,
"Well, don't listen to this guy.

00:02:19.536 --> 00:02:24.103
"His dad had a liquor store
and that's why he's successful."

00:02:24.103 --> 00:02:25.514
I was so scared of that, Dad.

00:02:25.514 --> 00:02:28.137
I was so scared of that 
in my teens and my 20s.

00:02:28.137 --> 00:02:30.072
It was the biggest fear I had.

00:02:30.072 --> 00:02:34.111
And now, as those 
negative comments

00:02:34.111 --> 00:02:36.371
or people that push back

00:02:36.371 --> 00:02:38.384
are the far minority,

00:02:38.384 --> 00:02:41.174
I find myself being 
passionate to make

00:02:41.174 --> 00:02:44.477
sure that your legacy isn't
lost and what you did isn't left

00:02:44.477 --> 00:02:48.848
behind and it doesn't become
the narrative of just what

00:02:48.848 --> 00:02:52.685
I've accomplished without the
context of what you accomplished

00:02:52.685 --> 00:02:54.710
and how much you 
helped me to get there.

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:57.758
And so, I want you to know that
and I want you know it now,

00:02:57.758 --> 00:03:02.224
not when you're 90 or 100 or 130

00:03:02.224 --> 00:03:04.464
when you're on your deathbed but

00:03:04.464 --> 00:03:08.521
I want you to know it now of
how much you mean to me and how

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:11.884
thankful I am and how much 
I learned from the way that you

00:03:11.884 --> 00:03:15.308
and mom and navigated and 
how I do think my hard work and

00:03:15.308 --> 00:03:18.891
my hustle is my separation
from the marketplace.

00:03:18.891 --> 00:03:19.992
And I know that's a learned

00:03:19.992 --> 00:03:22.781
behavior by watching 
how you did it.

00:03:22.781 --> 00:03:25.321
And I thank you from the 
bottom of my heart and so,

00:03:25.321 --> 00:03:28.771
I thought it was a
good time to say hey.

00:03:28.771 --> 00:03:30.359
I love you.

00:03:32.389 --> 00:03:33.838
(somber music)

00:03:40.202 --> 00:03:42.083
Thanks for being 
on the show, Dad.

00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:43.476
- You're welcome.

00:03:43.476 --> 00:03:46.337
(Gary laughing)

00:03:46.337 --> 00:03:51.733
A little bit of me.
- We're changing the wine world.

00:03:51.733 --> 00:03:56.028
- Who's more charismatic?
(Gary laughs)

00:03:56.028 --> 00:03:57.343
My son or me?

00:03:57.343 --> 00:03:59.466
(DRock laughs)
- Jesus.

00:03:59.466 --> 00:04:00.919
They're gonna love
you for this episode.

00:04:00.919 --> 00:04:03.169
You're gonna get more
votes that you deserve.

00:04:03.169 --> 00:04:05.819
(somber music)

